WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.900
- What does body positivity mean to you?

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.230
- You know, it's, it's interesting

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:05.580
'cause I feel like it's a term

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:07.670
that gets thrown around a lot

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:09.810
and it's sort of can be really simplified

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:11.310
and say like love yourself

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:15.330
and that's such a hard goal, you know?

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:16.720
And I think

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.110
body positivity to me is
exactly how we explore it

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:21.650
in Shrill, which is like

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:23.790
it's kind of this ongoing battle

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.170
and it's mostly internal.

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:29.910
It's like, how can you be
kinder to yourself and,

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:33.150
and be your own ally

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:35.840
as these external pressures come onto you.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.330
And I, you know, it's
certainly changed my life

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:40.450
because I, I cut myself some slack

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:43.310
and stopped being so tough on myself

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:45.780
and also tried to stop that constant loop

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.140
inside your head of being like,

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:49.250
oh I shouldn't sit like
this or I shouldn't eat that

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:52.120
or I don't want someone to
see me with my double chin.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:53.600
It's like, that's my reality

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:55.070
and I actually like myself

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:55.903
and
- Yeah.

00:00:55.903 --> 00:00:57.932
- it just makes life a lot better.

00:00:57.932 --> 00:00:58.870
(laughing)

00:00:58.870 --> 00:00:59.720
- No, I agree.

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:00.784
I, I love that definition.

00:01:00.784 --> 00:01:02.287
I have a very similar one.

